ITEM 97 -- wide-binary boost versus Galactocentric radius
====================================================================================================================
  El-Badry EDR3 catalogue: 1817594 pairs, 217 columns
  separation/chance-alignment columns present: ['sep_AU', 'R_chance_align']
  pairs with parallax > 2 mas (d < 500 pc) and parallax S/N > 20: 686496
  their distances span 3 - 500 pc; the Sun sits at R_GC = 8.2 kpc, so this sample spans
  R_GC = 7700 - 8700 pc at most -- a 12% range in Galactocentric radius.
  over that range the Milky Way's external field changes by only a factor 1.032 (deep-MOND g ~ 1/R), so the predicted
  change in the wide-binary boost is well under a percent -- far below the 2% systematic floor the frozen pre-registration carries.
  [PASS] 97 CANNOT be done with this catalogue and is recorded as underpowered, not as a null: the clean wide-binary sample lies within ~500 pc of the Sun, a 6% range in Galactocentric radius, over which the framework's predicted boost changes by under 1% against a 2% irreducible systematic   (sample spans 12% in R_GC; external field varies 3.2%; the frozen sigma_sys is 2%)
  what would make 97 live: Gaia DR4's fainter, more distant wide binaries (to 1-2 kpc) would give a 25-50% lever in R_GC --
  worth adding to the DR4 analysis as a SPLIT of the existing pre-registered statistic, not as a new prediction.

